! Proof Assistant session that creates dummy variables and then refers to
! one by name with LET VARIABLE.  The database also has an undeclared
! symbol, so the parser makes a placeholder token; placeholders and dummy
! variables are kept in separate g_MathToken[] slots, and this checks that
! a dummy variable is still found by its "$n" name when both are present.
prove th
assign 1 mp
show new_proof /all
let variable $2 = " p "
show new_proof /all
exit
